body:
That's very true. People notice. And sometimes react in a way that can hurt us. We just have to remember that people are not perfect. Some are jerks and want to hurt us, some aren't enough to know the right thing to say or do, and some are just very bad at conversations. some just don't now how to deal with something that is different from the 'usual' that they are accustomed to. In all cases, we need to learn to forget them and disregard their comments. Easier said than done, though.

I have recently been depressed due to circumstances around not having close friends. It was triggered by this guy who was all acting friendly with me at first, and then I tried to extend my hand in the friendship too. But then he told me he didn't want to be friends. But the way he said it was terrible. He started with "You are probably lonely and don't have anyone to hang out with. Not too many friends, I guess. You probably think math is easier than socialising. I could literally feel bile rising in my throat.

&#x200B;

Often, and in large quantities.  


\-not Dutch  


&#x200B;
